---
/* START HERE IS THE ONE PAGE THAT SAYS WHAT THIS IS. /start/ (three ways in) and /about/ (what it is, where it came from, what it does not
   know) were two pages with one job, and a visitor had to guess which to open. They are one page now, and /about/ redirects here.

   EVERY NUMBER ON THIS PAGE IS COUNTED, not typed (lib/start-data.js reads them from the same files the map and the other pages read). The page
   says what the map does not know, and a hand-written figure on it goes stale the first time a harvest runs, which is the failure it exists to
   catch. The same numbers fill the story tour (public/js/start-tour-gate.js opens it; /start-tour.html is its chapters).

   Everything is plain HTML in the page body: it reads, links and indexes with no script. The tour is an addition, not a gate. */
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { u } from "../lib/url.js";
import { startNumbers } from "../lib/start-data.js";
import { countries } from "../lib/inventory.js";
const n = startNumbers({ countriesKnown: countries });
---
<Base
  title="Start here"
  eyebrow="What this is, and what it does not know"
  dek="Where genealogical records are, who holds them and what it costs to look. Search any name a place has had.">

  <div class="k-hi st-hero" id="the-whole-page">
    <div class="st-hero-text">
      <p>My great-grandfather was born in Gallignana in 1863: where is that record, and can I see it tonight?</p>
      <p>That one question is what this atlas answers. It began as one family's archive and is open to the world. It is early, and says so.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="st-note" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="st-paper"><span class="st-hand">Gallignana</span><span class="st-hand st-hand-2">1863</span></div>
      <div class="st-stamp">= Gračišće</div>
      <div class="st-pin"></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <ul class="k-grid st-stats" aria-label="The atlas in numbers">
    <li class="k-card"><b>{n.places}</b><span>places</span></li>
    <li class="k-card"><b>{n.countries}</b><span>countries and territories</span></li>
    <li class="k-card"><b>{n.regions}</b><span>record regions</span></li>
    <li class="k-card"><b>{n.eras}</b><span>eras</span></li>
    <li class="k-card"><b>{n.volumes}</b><span>volumes</span></li>
    <li class="k-card is-warn"><b>{n.unsurveyedPct}%</b><span>not yet surveyed</span></li>
  </ul>

  <p class="st-play" id="story">
    <button type="button" class="st-playbtn" data-tour-open aria-haspopup="dialog">▶ Play the story <span class="st-key" aria-hidden="true">T</span></button>
    <span class="st-playnote">Two minutes, thirteen scenes, one invented grandmother. <a href={u("/")}>Or go straight to the map →</a></span>
  </p>

  <p class="st-story"><a href={u("/read/#story")}><b>Not sure where to start?</b> Tell us who you are looking for, in one sentence, and see their journey and a short plan →</a></p>

  <div class="k-bar"><h2>Three ways in</h2><span class="k-count">pick what you are holding</span></div>
  <ul class="k-grid st-ways">
    <li><a class="k-card" href={u("/?q=Gallignana")}><span class="k-pill">1 · A place name</span>
      <h3>Type it, even the old name</h3>
      <p>Gallignana finds Gračišće, Fiume finds Rijeka, Breslau finds Wrocław. {n.places} places, not just those with a shelf.</p></a></li>
    <li><a class="k-card" href={u("/?q=Xubrinich")}><span class="k-pill">2 · Only a surname</span>
      <h3>Type that instead</h3>
      <p>You get the other spellings, the countries where the name is attested, then the archives. Xubrinich answers Žubrinić.</p></a></li>
    <li><a class="k-card" href={u("/?layers=shelf,jurisdiction&years=1800,1920&view=45.1,14.3,8")}><span class="k-pill">3 · A place and years</span>
      <h3>Set the years</h3>
      <p>An 1863 baptism is in a Croatian archive; a 1930 one from the same village is filed under <em>Italy</em>. A range that crosses a handover is where records get lost.</p></a></li>
  </ul>

  <div class="k-bar"><h2>Four things stand between you and the record</h2></div>
  <ol class="st-four">
    <li class="k-card"><h3>The name changed</h3><p>Gallignana is Gračišće. The find box matches every name a place has had: {n.altPlaces} places and {n.altNames} other names.</p></li>
    <li class="k-card"><h3>The jurisdiction changed</h3><p>A 1930 record from the same village may be filed under <em>Italy</em>. <a href={u("/providers/#regions")}>See the table →</a></p></li>
    <li class="k-card"><h3>“Online” is eight things</h3><p>Free images, a login, an index only, part paid, paywall, a catalogue card, in the building, and, for {n.unsurveyedPct}% of places, nobody has looked.</p></li>
    <li class="k-card"><h3>It is not always a register</h3><p>Australia has no parish registers. {n.newspapers} digitised newspapers are the record for most ancestors before 1950.</p></li>
  </ol>

  <div class="k-hi is-plain st-colours">
    <p>What the colours mean</p>
    <p>Each dot is coloured by what it would cost you to look right now. Nothing else is ever coloured, and each panel says the same in words.</p>
    <ul class="st-key-chips" aria-label="The colours, named">
      <li style="--k: var(--acc-free)">Free images</li>
      <li style="--k: var(--acc-account)">Free login</li>
      <li style="--k: var(--acc-index)">Index only</li>
      <li style="--k: var(--acc-paid)">Paywall</li>
      <li style="--k: var(--acc-catalogue)">Catalogue card</li>
      <li style="--k: var(--acc-onsite)">In a building</li>
      <li style="--k: var(--acc-unsurveyed)">Nobody has looked</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="k-bar"><h2>Three doors</h2></div>
  <ul class="k-grid st-doors">
    <li><a class="k-card" href={u("/your-name/")}><span class="k-ico" aria-hidden="true">🔎</span><h3>Type a name</h3>
      <p>{n.surnameFamilies} families of spellings and {n.givenNames} given names in {n.givenForms} forms: Ivan, Johann and Giovanni are one name.</p></a></li>
    <li><a class="k-card" href={u("/tree-canvas/")}><span class="k-ico" aria-hidden="true">🌳</span><h3>Drop in a tree</h3>
      <p>A GEDCOM, read in your browser: your tree as a tree, a fan, lifespans or place lanes, and where it needs tidying.</p></a></li>
    <li><a class="k-card" href={u("/read/#story")}><span class="k-ico" aria-hidden="true">✎</span><h3>Tell a story</h3>
      <p>Who you are looking for, in a sentence. It draws the journey and gives a short plan.</p></a></li>
  </ul>
  <ul class="k-pills st-also" aria-label="Also">
    <li><a class="k-pill is-plain" href={u("/")}>The map</a></li>
    <li><a class="k-pill is-plain" href={u("/read/")}>Record Reader · {n.terms} terms</a></li>
    <li><a class="k-pill is-plain" href={u("/flags/")}>Flags</a></li>
    <li><a class="k-pill is-plain" href={u("/history/")}>History</a></li>
    <li><a class="k-pill is-plain" href={u("/connect/")}>Connect to the data</a></li>
    <li><a class="k-pill is-plain" href={u("/providers/#regions")}>{n.regions} record regions</a></li>
    <li><a class="k-pill is-plain" href={u("/surnames/")}>The surname dataset</a></li>
  </ul>

  <div class="k-bar"><h2>Whose flag flew over it</h2></div>
  <div class="k-hi is-plain">
    <p>{n.flagPages} pages of flag history say who governed which ground, and when. This atlas knows which archive each regime’s paper went to: {n.eras} eras in {n.regions} regions, with the flags grouped into {n.hubs} hubs.</p>
    <p>The two sit side by side and are not yet one search. <a href={u("/flags/")}>Open the flags →</a></p>
  </div>

  <div class="k-bar"><h2>Where it came from</h2></div>
  <div class="k-hi is-plain">
    <p>Out of <a href="https://daviddef.github.io/TheDefranceski/map/">one family’s archive</a>. Its Croatian depth ({n.hrPlaces} places, {n.hrVolumes} volumes) is that archive’s work, imported once; what was family-specific was dropped.</p>
    <p>There are <a href={u("/my-work/")}>{n.archivesWord} such archives</a>, and what they share is why this atlas exists.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="k-bar"><h2>What it does not know</h2></div>
  <div class="k-hi">
    <p><b>{n.unsurveyedPct}% of the ground on this map has never been surveyed.</b></p>
    <p>Of {n.places} dots in {n.countriesWithDots} countries, only {n.walked} (in {n.walkedCountries} countries) have been walked volume by volume. A grey dot means nobody has looked, never that nothing is there.</p>
  </div>
  <ul class="k-grid st-know">
    <li class="k-card"><h3>Regions follow the research</h3><p>Each was written because someone was stuck on that ground and needed to know whose archive to write to.</p></li>
    <li class="k-card"><h3>Unopened sources are listed as such</h3><p>{n.sourcesUnopened} of {n.sources} sources were named by a register or open dataset and nobody has opened them yet. {n.sourcesOpened} have had their door tried; none is called surveyed until someone has read it.</p></li>
    <li class="k-card"><h3>Declined is a result</h3><p>{n.declined} sources were assessed and turned down, with the reason written out. A bot gate is never worked around.</p></li>
  </ul>
  <details class="k-more st-more">
    <summary><span class="k-mt">The longer account</span></summary>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>The regions were chosen by where research is being done, not by what would look impressive on a map. A place outside a mapped region says so in its own panel rather than guessing.</p>
      <p>Keeping “nobody has surveyed it” apart from “nothing is there” is worth more than coverage: a map that quietly implies completeness sends people home when they should keep looking.</p>
      <p>An archive that refuses a robot is stating terms, and an atlas that asks archives to trust it cannot be the thing that ignores them.</p>
    </div>
  </details>
  <ul class="k-pills st-also">
    <li><a class="k-pill" href={u("/coverage/")}>See exactly how incomplete it is →</a></li>
    <li><a class="k-pill is-plain" href={u("/add/")}>Add a source we lack</a></li>
  </ul>

  <div class="k-bar"><h2>How it is built</h2></div>
  <ul class="k-grid st-know">
    <li class="k-card"><h3>A static site</h3><p>No server, no database, no account. The data is plain JSON <a href={n.repo}>in a public repository</a>. Your research stays in your own browser unless you choose to back it up.</p></li>
    <li class="k-card"><h3>Gated before it ships</h3><p>The build refuses a source with no date, a provider that does not resolve, or coordinates in the wrong country. That last gate caught the Carnia comuni filed as Croatian.</p></li>
    <li class="k-card"><h3>Downloaded, not scraped</h3><p>Outlines are Natural Earth, the gazetteer is GeoNames (CC BY 4.0), maps are OpenStreetMap. Historical regions are drawn by hand, roughly, to say which filing system applied, not to settle a border.</p></li>
  </ul>

  <div class="k-bar"><h2>Behind the atlas</h2></div>
  <ul class="k-pills st-also">
    <li><a class="k-pill is-plain" href={u("/worklist/")}>What is being done</a></li>
    <li><a class="k-pill is-plain" href={u("/errands/")}>Letters to send</a></li>
    <li><a class="k-pill is-plain" href={u("/my-work/")}>My work</a></li>
    <li><a class="k-pill is-plain" href={u("/changelog/")}>What changed</a></li>
  </ul>
</Base>

<style>
  .st-hero { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 280px); gap: 28px; align-items: center; padding: 28px 32px; max-width: none; border-radius: 28px;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--hue-wash), var(--panel)); }
  .st-hero p:first-child { font-size: clamp(24px, 3.2vw, 36px); font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.2; letter-spacing: -.02em; }
  .st-hero p + p { margin-top: 14px; }
  .st-note { position: relative; height: 190px; }
  .st-paper { position: absolute; inset: 8px 14px 14px 10px; transform: rotate(-4deg); background: #EADFC6; color: #3a2c17; border-radius: 4px; box-shadow: 0 10px 22px rgba(0,0,0,.28), inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(0,0,0,.06); display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: center; gap: 4px; padding: 0 18px;
    background-image: repeating-linear-gradient(to bottom, transparent 0 27px, rgba(80,60,30,.18) 27px 28px); }
  .st-hand { font: italic 600 30px/1.1 var(--serif); color: #2b2113; }
  .st-hand-2 { font-size: 22px; opacity: .75; }
  .st-stamp { position: absolute; right: -2px; bottom: 6px; transform: rotate(6deg); font: 700 13px/1 var(--mono); letter-spacing: .06em; color: #8f3a1a; border: 2px solid #8f3a1a; border-radius: 6px; padding: 6px 9px; background: #EADFC6; }
  .st-pin { position: absolute; top: 0; left: 50%; width: 14px; height: 14px; margin-left: -7px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--hue); box-shadow: 0 2px 4px rgba(0,0,0,.4); }
  @media (max-width: 640px) { .st-hero { grid-template-columns: 1fr; padding: 20px; } .st-note { height: 150px; max-width: 260px; } }

  .st-stats { grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 118px), 1fr)); margin: 0 0 22px; }
  .st-stats .k-card { padding: 12px 14px; gap: 2px; border-radius: 16px; }
  .st-stats b { font: 800 clamp(24px, 2.6vw, 32px)/1.05 var(--serif); letter-spacing: -.02em; color: var(--hue-ink); }
  .st-stats span { font: 600 11px/1.3 var(--sans); letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-2); }
  .st-stats .is-warn { border-top-color: var(--rule-strong); }

  .st-play { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 10px 18px; margin: 4px 0 14px; scroll-margin-top: 80px; }
  .st-playbtn { font: 700 17px/1 var(--sans); display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; cursor: pointer; border: 0; background: var(--hue-solid); color: var(--on-hue); border-radius: 999px; padding: 14px 26px; min-height: 48px; box-shadow: 0 10px 22px -10px var(--hue-solid); }
  .st-playbtn:hover { filter: brightness(1.08); }
  .st-playbtn:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid var(--hue); outline-offset: 3px; }
  .st-key { font: 500 11px/1 var(--mono, monospace); border: 1px solid currentColor; border-radius: 4px; padding: 3px 6px; opacity: .85; }
  .st-playnote { flex: 1 1 18rem; font: 400 14px/1.5 var(--sans); color: var(--ink-2); }
  .st-story { margin: 0 0 8px; padding: 14px 20px; background: var(--hue-wash); border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--hue) 25%, var(--rule)); border-radius: 18px; font: 400 16px/1.45 var(--sans); }
  .st-story a { color: var(--ink); text-decoration: none; } .st-story b { color: var(--hue-ink); }

  .st-ways, .st-doors, .st-know { margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .st-ways li, .st-doors li { display: flex; }
  .st-ways .k-card, .st-doors .k-card { flex: 1; align-items: flex-start; gap: 8px; }
  .st-ways .k-card p, .st-doors .k-card p, .st-four p, .st-know p { font-size: 14px; }
  .st-ways h3, .st-doors h3 { font-size: 21px; }
  .st-ways .k-pill { align-self: flex-start; }
  .st-doors .k-ico { width: 48px; height: 48px; font-size: 24px; }

  .st-four { list-style: none; margin: 0 0 8px; padding: 0; counter-reset: four; display: grid; gap: 14px; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 280px), 1fr)); }
  .st-four li { counter-increment: four; padding-left: 70px; min-height: 96px; }
  .st-four li::before { content: counter(four); position: absolute; left: 18px; top: 12px; font: 800 44px/1 var(--serif); color: var(--hue-ink); opacity: .9; }
  .st-four h3 { font-size: 19px; }
  .st-know { grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 260px), 1fr)); }
  .st-know h3 { font-size: 19px; }

  .st-colours { max-width: none; border-radius: 18px; margin-top: 22px; }
  .st-key-chips { list-style: none; margin: 14px 0 0; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }
  .st-key-chips li { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; padding: 5px 12px 5px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--rule-strong); border-radius: 999px; background: var(--panel); font: 600 13px/1 var(--sans); color: var(--ink); }
  .st-key-chips li::before { content: ""; width: 14px; height: 14px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--k); border: 2px solid var(--ink-2); box-sizing: border-box; }   /* the ring keeps the dark greens visible on the dark ground */

  .st-also { margin: 14px 0 6px; }
  .st-more { margin: 10px 0 8px; max-width: 78ch; }
  .st-more .prose p { font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--ink-2); margin: 0 0 10px; }
  main .k-hi { max-width: none; border-radius: 18px; }
</style>
